WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:03.503
I am from Bermuda,
and so we wore school uniforms.

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:05.938
In high school,
I went on a crusade

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:08.141
<i> to allow women to wear pants.</i>

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:10.610
So I've always been
very focused on

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:12.545
<i> the narrative
 that our clothing takes.</i>

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:14.981
♪ (UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:16.382 line:0%
I'm Shiona Turini,

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:19.018 line:0%
and I am the costume designer
of<i> Insecure.</i>

00:00:19.118 --> 00:00:20.953
<i> I always wanted to work
 in fashion,</i>

00:00:21.053 --> 00:00:22.789
<i> there was no other option
 for me.</i>

00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:23.956
<i> I moved to New York,</i>

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:26.592
<i> and I started to work in
 the editorial capacity,</i>

00:00:26.692 --> 00:00:29.195
<i> and then I did a few
 music videos here and there.</i>

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:32.065
I was one of the stylists
for Beyoncé's "Formation,"

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:35.334
Solange Knowles' "Cranes,"
and "Don't Touch My Hair."

00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:38.538
<i> Eventually I was put on a job
 with Issa Rae.</i>

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:42.041
<i> And they contacted me
to see if I would be interested</i>

00:00:42.141 --> 00:00:44.744
<i> in costume designing
 for</i> Insecure.

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:45.845
And I said yes.

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:51.384
<i> It is such an honor to be
 with a team that's led by</i>

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:53.820
so many women,
especially women of color.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:57.757
<i> As a black woman,
diversity is always top of mind.</i>

00:00:57.857 --> 00:01:01.127
<i> We try and include
 black designers
 on every single episode.</i>

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:03.763
<i> It's important and it's
 our social responsibility</i>

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:07.099
to make sure that we are
highlighting talented people

00:01:07.199 --> 00:01:08.200
on and off camera.

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:12.004
<i> When I started at</i> Insecure,
<i> the aesthetics
 of the main characters</i>

00:01:12.104 --> 00:01:14.006
<i> were pretty much already
 carved out,</i>

00:01:14.106 --> 00:01:15.875
which was a unique challenge,

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:18.143
because I continued
that narrative,

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:20.079
<i>but added my own personal touch.</i>

00:01:20.746 --> 00:01:23.182
<i> I feel deeply connected
 to the material.</i>

00:01:23.282 --> 00:01:26.052
<i> It's telling our stories
 as black women.</i>

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:29.121
<i> It's just an honor
 to be a part of that team</i>

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:32.158
that is releasing this baby
into the world.

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:33.760
♪ (MUSIC CONCLUDES) ♪

